{"availability":"available","full":"ubisoft/ubisoft-laforge-Poisson-Filters","name":"ubisoft-laforge-Poisson-Filters","description":"Compact Poisson Filters for Fast Fluid Simulation","category":"Other","language":"HLSL","stars":90,"forks":10,"created":"2023-05-23T15:47:57Z","updated":"2025-06-28T04:49:08Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3528233.3530737","topics":["fluid-simulation"],"demo":"https://www.shahinrabbani.ca/poissonfilters.html","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:19:12.067Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T22:19:12.067Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T22:19:12.067Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T00:30:30.765Z","stars":90,"forks":10},{"at":"2026-10-10T06:59:42.188Z","stars":90,"forks":10},{"at":"2026-10-15T21:43:55.710Z","stars":90,"forks":10},{"at":"2026-10-19T22:19:12.067Z","stars":90,"forks":10}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Compact Poisson filters are powerful alternatives to iterative linear methods to solve \\ Poisson's equation $\\nabla^{2} \\phi = f$, particularly for real-time applications, where interactivity is of high importance.","Poisson filter-based method is a one-shot, convolutional linear solver that balances between the strengths of spectral and iterative methods with a parallel implementation on GPU. Our solver precludes the need for careful preconditioning, scales favorably with the size of the problem, handles Neumann boundary conditions, and is a drop-in replacement with controllable error tolerance for existing solvers in high-performance settings.","While the main application presented in this work is enhancing the runtime performance of Eulerian fluids simulation, Poisson filters have the potential to be used in other domains that require a fast solution to Poisson's equation, such as image processing, cloth simulation, Newtonian gravity, and electrostatics."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ubisoft/ubisoft-laforge-Poisson-Filters/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d81905fcd94c9c7685a6bbdf2834ed3622bceb01d363264049e749d9e0570d1a","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T00:30:30.890Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T00:30:30.890Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Compact Poisson filters are powerful alternatives to iterative linear methods to solve \\ Poisson's equation $\\nabla^{2} \\phi = f$, particularly for real-time applications, where interactivity is of high importance.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ubisoft/ubisoft-laforge-Poisson-Filters/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"d81905fcd94c9c7685a6bbdf2834ed3622bceb01d363264049e749d9e0570d1a","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ubisoft/ubisoft-laforge-Poisson-Filters/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T00:30:30.890Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2025-06-28T04:49:08Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ubisoft/ubisoft-laforge-Poisson-Filters/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T00:30:30.890Z","hash":"d81905fcd94c9c7685a6bbdf2834ed3622bceb01d363264049e749d9e0570d1a","originalBytes":4856,"storedBytes":4856,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T00:30:30.765Z","subjects":["Simulation & physics"],"platforms":[],"classification":{"version":4,"method":"local_rules","category":"Other","subjects":["Simulation & physics"],"evidence":[{"subject":"Simulation & physics","source":"metadata","match":"Simulation"}],"platformEvidence":[],"platformSupport":"author_metadata_not_runtime_tested","suggestedSubjects":["Science"],"reviewRequired":true},"demoHealth":{"url":"https://www.shahinrabbani.ca/poissonfilters.html","attemptedAt":"2026-10-15T02:19:09.224Z","probeVersion":3,"status":"working","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T02:19:09.224Z","lastWorkingAt":"2026-10-15T02:19:09.224Z","target":"https://www.shahinrabbani.ca/poissonfilters.html","failureCount":0,"consecutiveTemporaryFailures":0,"nextCheckAt":"2026-10-22T02:19:09.224Z"},"previ